+    * blocks decode differently (sign extension, mode selection), so it gets a
+    * second decoded copy, decoded as bc_alt (VK_FORMAT_UNDEFINED when there
+    * is none) and stored as bc_alt_format. It is laid out, bound and written
+    * like bc_decoded (bc_alt_shadow on the fragment path), bc_alt_offset
+    * bytes after the image base. */
+   VkFormat bc_alt;
